  {
    "sha": "e8f8d3b2cecd89369f9ed519f89a6ae5a02b2e43",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV5OD-doAKGU4ZjhkM2IyY2VjZDg5MzY5ZjllZDUxOWY4OWE2YWU1YTAyYjJlNDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T04:11:43Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T04:11:43Z"
      },
      "message": "perf(sim): grow the column stock's cut history in place\n\ncut::simulate copied the stock's whole cut history at the start of each\ncall. A caller that cuts one move for each call thus copied a longer\nhistory at each step, and the time was quadratic in the moves.\n\nThe history is now taken out, grown with Arc::make_mut (a copy only when\nanother stock shares it) and put back. On a refusal, the cuts are\ntruncated to their old count and the history goes back, because add_ops\nonly appends cuts.\n\nPinned by stock_sim::cut::history_tests (the history keeps its\nallocation across calls; a clone keeps its own history and columns) and\nstock_columns::one_move_for_each_call_is_the_one_call_cut (4000\none-move calls give the one-call stock to the bit).\n\nFixes #3819\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "0c3fb6550030d84bfdad80abdeabe8745a948e8a",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/0c3fb6550030d84bfdad80abdeabe8745a948e8a"
